cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Can LLMs Produce Contrarian Ideas?"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: jay-azhang
repository-code: "https://github.com/jay-azhang/can-llms-produce-contrarian-ideas"
url: "https://jay-azhang.github.io/can-llms-produce-contrarian-ideas/"
abstract: >-
  1,305 responses from nine frontier language models across eight labs, asked
  under twelve prompt framings — seven for a belief others reject, five for an
  idea the model originated — each graded by three independent models on
  specialist agreement, public agreement, originality and social cost.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - output diversity
  - model homogeneity
  - evaluation
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
